        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 68-year-old male admitted on 16/03/2021 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Blood tests revealed mild inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and pulse oximetry monitoring throughout the stay. Clinical response was satisfactory with improvement of respiratory function. He is discharged in stable condition with oral prednisolone taper and inhaler optimisation. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Discharge diagnosis: COPD with acute exacerbation (ICD-10: J44.1).</div>"
            },
